rectangle of 0s that is at least 2 cells tall and 2 cells wide.\n2. Paint that rectangle 2.\n3. Repeat until no such rectangle is left.\n\n**Checking it against the demonstrations by hand:**\n- **Pair 3:** the 4×2 block (area 8) beats the overlapping 2×3 (area 6). Once it is painted, the leftover column x = 12 is only 1 cell wide, so it stays 0. This is exactly the cell that was wrong before.\n- **Pair 1:** at rows 3–4, x = 6..8, the 2×3 block is the largest rectangle in that patch. The 3×2 block at rows 4–6, x = 11..12 cannot grow any wider.\n- **Pair 1, two separate squares:** the two 2×2 squares in the big bottom-left component do not overlap, so the repeat step paints both of them.\n- **Earlier result:** the window rule was already exact on pairs 1 and 2, and those pairs contain no overlap conflict. The greedy version should give the same result there.\n\nThese checks were done by eye. The new program has not been run yet; the verifier will confirm whether it reproduces all three train pairs.\n\n**Test input:** the same procedure is applied. Each solid block of 0s, at least 2×2, is painted 2, largest first. Thinner leftovers stay 0.\n\n**Emit stages:** I emit once after each rectangle is painted, then emit the final grid.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    vals = [v for v in np.unique(g) if v != bg]\n    fg = vals[0] if vals else 0\n    H, W = g.shape\n    out = g.copy()\n    avail = (g == fg)\n    while True:\n        P = np.zeros((H + 1, W + 1), dtype=int)\n        P[1:, 1:] = np.cumsum(np.cumsum(avail.astype(int), 0), 1)\n        best = None\n        for y0 in range(H):\n            for y1 in range(y0 + 1, H):\n                h = y1 - y0 + 1\n                for x0 in range(W):\n                    for x1 in range(x0 + 1, W):\n                        w = x1 - x0 + 1\n                        s = P[y1+1, x1+1] - P[y0, x1+1] - P[y1+1, x0] + P[y0, x0]\n                        if s != h * w:\n                            break\n                        if best is None or h * w > best[0]:\n                            best = (h * w, y0, x0, y1, x1)\n        if best is None:\n            break\n        _, y0, x0, y1, x1 = best\n        out[y0:y1+1, x0:x1+1] = 2\n        avail[y0:y1+1, x0:x1+1] = False\n        emit(out.copy(), f\"Largest remaining solid block of {fg}s ({y1-y0+1}x{x1-x0+1} at rows {y0}-{y1}, cols {x0}-{x1}) recoloured 2.\")\n    emit(out, \"No solid block of at least 2x2 remains; final grid.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"When rectangles overlap, only the largest one is painted, and the smaller overlapping one loses."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Revised rule (greedy largest rectangles):**"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Among cells that are still 0, find the largest-area solid rectangle of 0s that is at least 2 cells tall and 2 cells wide."}],"recolour":[{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Largest remaining solid block of 0s (2x3 at rows 3-4, cols 6-8) recoloured 2."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Largest remaining solid block of 0s (3x2 at rows 4-6, cols 11-12) recoloured 2."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Largest remaining solid block of 0s (2x2 at rows 1-2, cols 13-14) recoloured 2."}],"order":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each solid block of 0s, at least 2×2, is painted 2, largest first."}],"layers":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"When rectangles overlap, only the largest one is painted, and the smaller overlapping one loses."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- **Pair 3:** the 4×2 block (area 8) beats the overlapping 2×3 (area 6)."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"63284d70d9fe04a4055f518c5820f18305239a036a2efbb8af15de835d81f74a","task_sha256":"980f74056699c5a675a023f3ed241c66ff2f88a85260f453c7667231cf8cb134","validation":"Frozen corpus 